  data:  # cdc0
    kind: work_item  # cdc0
    title: "The section 3a coverage gate keys on CALL nodes, so a def/use omission at a non-call construct still licenses an unearned False (INV-lupav L2 residual; price the widened forfeit share before widening)"  # cdc0
    status: todo_hard  # cdc0
    priority: 2  # cdc0
    parent:  # cdc0
    tags:  # cdc0
    - taint  # cdc0
    - adr_0017  # cdc0
    - dataflow  # cdc0
    isbefore: []  # cdc0
    duplicate_of: []  # cdc0
    not_duplicate_of: []  # cdc0
    pr_ref:  # cdc0
    description: "INV-lupav's clause L2, intact after every fix shipped for it, reached through\nthe one hole WI-joluk's coverage gate is built not to see.\n\nTHE GATE ASKS ONE QUESTION: does every CALL node in the function body sit\ninside a recorded CFG statement extent (cfg.uncovered_call_lines)? A def/use\nomission at a construct that is NOT a call is therefore invisible to it, and\nthe walk exhausts and returns False -- which since WI-kabif (2026-09-02)\nREMOVES the flow.\n\nMEASURED, not read off the source. Probe at dev 79961e513f with the control\nfirst, production summaries loaded:\n\n    L1 cwd := src()\n    L2 a := cwd                  recorded; single heir; tracked\n    L3 print(a)                  terminating summary\n    L4 for _, c := range cwd {   SECOND use of cwd -- invisible (WI-losod)\n    L5     sink(c)               sink, and this call IS covered\n\n    CONTROL (second use recorded)      -> True   ADMISSIBLE\n    RESIDUAL (second use unrecorded)   -> False  <- true answer is True\n    RESIDUAL, forfeit_refutation=True  -> None\n\nEvery heir is tracked, so INV-lupav's heir-granularity fix has no subject.\nEvery call is covered, so the gate has no subject. The omission is a missing\nUSE at a non-call construct, and nothing in the pipeline can currently see it.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT JUST \"WIDEN THE PREDICATE\" -- THE DESIGN QUESTION TO SETTLE\nFIRST. WI-joluk pre-registered the forfeit share as the number that decides\nwhether refutation is worth having: 12.8% to 35.5% across five repo-language\npairs, \"not near 100%, so refutation stays viable on the remainder\". Widening\ncoverage from CALL nodes to every statement-bearing construct will raise that\nshare, and if it approaches 100% then section 3a removal authority -- granted\n2026-09-02 -- is worth nothing, because every function forfeits. So the first\ndeliverable here is the MEASUREMENT of the widened share on the same five\npairs, and the decision is the owner's, not the implementation's. Do not widen\nthe predicate and ship it; price it first.\n\nBLAST RADIUS TODAY IS ZERO AND THAT IS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. Section 3a\nreturns False zero times in production: 84 walks on hypergumbo-core (29 True /\n55 None / 0 False) and 22 on alertmanager (8 True / 14 None / 0 False), every\nwalk wrapped and tallied over real verify-claims runs. Escapes dominate, which\nis INV-busis from the other side. This class activates as escape sites close,\nwhich is exactly when the unearned False starts deleting findings.\n\nPRIORITY NOTE FOR THE OWNER. Filed P2 to match INV-lupav, but the two legs\ndiffer: INV-lupav was re-ranked P0->P2 on 2026-08-17 partly because it \"cannot\nbe worked\" (both of its blockers, WI-joluk and WI-kabif, are now done, so that\nleg has expired). This item CAN be worked and still changes nothing today."  # cdc0
    fields: {}  # cdc0
