  message: "Filed out of INV-lupav's thread on 2026-09-14 alongside PR #957, which closed\nthe heir-granularity route and left this one open. The probe in the\ndescription was run at dev 79961e513f with the positive control first and is\nreproduced in that PR's commit body."  # 0699
- op: discuss  # a11b
  at: '2026-09-14T23:09:12Z'  # a11b
  by: agent  # a11b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a11b
  clock: 4  # a11b
  nonce: a11b  # a11b
  message: "PHASE 1 DONE: THE WIDENED SHARE IS PRICED, AND IT IS NOT NEAR 100%.\n\nINSTRUMENT. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/meas/\nforfeit_share_widened.py -- a SIBLING of the 2026-08-06 forfeit_share.py that\nproduced WI-joluk's original numbers, not an edit of it. It IMPORTS that\nfile's controls, fixtures and exclusion set rather than re-deriving them, and\nthe baseline arm calls production cfg.uncovered_call_lines. Denominator is\nfunctions producing DDG edges, matching ddg_build.py:265-272 and WI-joluk's\nown denominator, so the two numbers are comparable rather than merely\nadjacent.\n\nFLOOR CHECK FIRST -- can each candidate predicate return \"covered\" AT ALL? A\ngate that cannot pass is not a gate.\n    PASS  ident  uncovered=3   covered=0\n    PASS  leaf   uncovered=3   covered=0\n    FAIL  named  uncovered=13  covered=2   <- VOIDED\n\"named\" (any uncovered named node) fires on a FULLY COVERED function, because\nthe function BODY node is contained in no statement extent by construction. It\nreads as a 100% forfeit on every repo, which looks like a finding and is an\nartefact. It is reported voided rather than quoted.\n\nFORFEIT SHARE, WI-joluk's own five pairs:\n    repo          lang     walkable   current   ident    leaf\n    alertmanager  go           1271     32.3%   44.9%   45.4%\n    prometheus    go           4428     36.2%   52.8%   53.3%\n    kserve        go           1555     27.7%   43.0%   43.0%\n    kserve        python       1358     29.1%   37.5%   37.5%\n    hypergumbo    python      28621     12.5%   18.8%   18.8%\n\nBASELINE HAS NOT DRIFTED. The current column reproduces WI-joluk's recorded\n33.5 / 35.5 / 26.9 / 27.8 / 12.8. That is the control on the instrument\nitself: a baseline arm that failed to reproduce would void the widened arm.\n\nTHE ANSWER TO THE PRE-REGISTERED QUESTION. WI-joluk registered \"not near 100%,\nso refutation stays viable on the remainder\" as the condition. Widened, the\nshare is 18.8%-53.3%, so refutation survives on 46.7%-81.2% of walkable\nfunctions. The fork this item was filed to expose -- that closing INV-lupav\nmight cost WI-kabif's removal authority -- is NOT forced by the number.\n\nAND THE GRAMMAR-NEUTRAL SPELLING IS FREE. \"leaf\" (named, childless, not\ncomment or punctuation -- reusing the shipped non-semantic skip list at\ncfg.py:857-862) costs essentially nothing over the substring test on\n\"identifier\": identical on three of five pairs, +0.5pp on the other two. So\nthe predicate needs no new per-language vocabulary AND gives up no precision\nfor doing without one. That removes the last argument for a declared\nnode-type list.\n\nNOT YET DECIDED HERE, deliberately: whether 53.3% on prometheus -- more than\nhalf of all walkable functions forfeiting -- is worth paying even though it is\nnot near 100%, and whether WI-losod (which would buy the share back rather\nthan forfeit it) is the better spend. Those are judgment, not measurement, and\nthe numbers above are what they should be judged against."  # a11b
